course: dictionary
lesson: 1072
title: Bout: a short spell
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bout is a short period of something, such as an illness or a strong feeling. Look at the words around it: «a few bouts of tonsillitis» means a few short spells of sore, swollen tonsils, not one long illness that never ends.
explain: The words after "of" are your clues. A bout of flu, a bout of laughter and a bout of exercise each tell you what the bout is about. Try the swap check: "a short spell of flu" still makes sense, so bout means a short spell.
explain: Bout has a second meaning in sport. A boxing or wrestling bout is a match between two fighters. Ask yourself: are the words about feeling ill, feeling happy, or fighting in a ring? The context tells you which meaning to use.
fact: A bout is a short period of something, such as an illness or a strong feeling.
fact: «A few bouts of tonsillitis» means a few short spells of sore, swollen tonsils.
fact: Tonsils are lumps at the back of the throat that help fight germs.
fact: A bout of giggles is a short fit of giggling.
fact: In sport, a bout is a boxing or wrestling match between two people.
exercise: «She had a bout of flu last week and stayed in bed.» What does bout mean here? | *A short spell of illness | A school trip | A long holiday | A big family meal
exercise: Ellie had a bout of giggles in class. What does bout mean? | A set of school rules | *A short fit of giggling | A boxing match | A long lesson
exercise: Which phrase names a short spell of illness? | *a bout of flu | a bunch of grapes | a pair of socks
test: What does a bout of exercise mean? | A bag full of gym kit | *A short time of hard exercise | A place to exercise | A long rest at home
test: What is a bout in a boxing ring? | A cough | A short sleep | *A match between two fighters
exam: Which meaning of bout fits «a bout of giggles»? | *A short period of a strong feeling | A plate of food | A boxing match | A long journey
